From ca40ca70b4ae9f58c766edf37d02a687bd81c494 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 16:32:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restructure into the festim_microstructure package described
 in the README

Library code moves under src/festim_microstructure/ and every script becomes
either a module there or a thin driver under examples/. Nothing importable
is left at the repository root.

Shared core (previously duplicated across 2-5 scripts):
  subdomains.py        GrainBoundaryNetwork (geometric locator, with the
                       interior-facet drop from micromodel.py) and
                       TaggedGrainBoundaryNetwork (facet tags); Grain,
                       GrainSurface
  solvers.py           ATOL, DIRECT_SOLVER_OPTIONS, tune_direct_solver
  models/properties.py Physics, crystal_diffusivity_field, one
                       gb_diffusivity_field(network, theta, ...)
  models/fisher.py     ShortCircuitProblem: the single-lattice + network model
                       that voronoi_2d/3d, neper and ebsd each re-implemented
  postprocessing/measures.py  inventory, submesh_measure, component_count
                       (2D/3D), junction_only_below

Meshing:
  meshing/voronoi.py   gb_homogenisation/microstructure.py, plus the 3D
                       geometry from voronoi_polycrystal_3d.py; the class is
                       VoronoiMicrostructure; `fm-voronoi` CLI; gmsh/dolfinx
                       imported lazily so the tessellation geometry is
                       importable and testable without them
  meshing/neper.py     run_neper (NeperOptions), StatFile, NeperMicrostructure,
                       read_mesh, and mesh_tesr(), a Python port of
                       ebsd_to_mesh.sh; dolfinx imported lazily
  meshing/ebsd/        the EBSD modules with relative imports;
                       ebsd_gb_diffusion.py becomes pipeline.py
                       (EbsdOptions, EbsdMicrostructure, run_ebsd_pipeline,
                       `fm-ebsd` CLI)
  _binaries.py         find_binary(): explicit path -> FM_NEPER_BIN /
                       FM_GMSH_BIN / FM_POVRAY_BIN -> PATH. The hard-coded
                       /home/fenna/... paths are gone.

Models:
  models/resolved.py        micromodel.py minus the extracted pieces; the
                            docstring and NOTE/TODO edits from 3809b5e are
                            carried into whichever module each piece moved to
  models/homogenisation.py  homogenise.py (`fm-homogenise`)
  models/validation.py      validate.py (`fm-validate`)
  models/diaz_rodriguez*.py the two root scripts; the mesh is now built by
                            make_mesh() from run()/main() instead of at import
  postprocessing/figures.py plots.py

Examples are rewritten as a Setup dataclass plus main(): no module-level
execution, no sys.path.insert, no import-time matplotlib backend selection.
Data files move to examples/data/, the homogenisation write-up to docs/.

Packaging: pillow declared (micrograph.py imports PIL), unused pandas
dropped, console-script targets point at modules that exist,
setuptools_scm's _version.py and bytecode are ignored, committed .pyc files
removed.

Tests: orientation conventions, Voronoi geometry, Neper stat readers, an
import walk of every submodule (with dolfinx/festim stubbed when absent),
and a FEniCS end-to-end smoke test that skips without dolfinx.

Behaviour changes to be aware of:
- GrainBoundaryNetwork drops facets on the outer boundary by default, as
  micromodel.py did; voronoi_polycrystal_2d.py previously did not.
- build_mesh() tags one physical group per Voronoi cell (from
  microstructure.py) where voronoi_polycrystal_2d.py tagged a single group.
- Grain.locate_subdomain_entities keeps its `mesh` argument. 3809b5e
  dropped it, but FESTIM passes the mesh to this hook (GrainBoundaryNetwork
  in the same file still takes it), so the one-argument form would fail at
  initialise().
